24:     Rule
25:     - For each control pixel, cast rays in both directions perpendicular to the bars.
26:     - Stop each ray at the first bar cell it reaches and color the control-to-hit segment with the control color.
27:     - After all rays are drawn, stamp a 3x3 block of the bar color centered on each hit, restoring the center to the control color.
28:     - Directions with no bar before the grid edge emit nothing.
29: 
30:     Key insight
31:     - The only complete rows or columns identify the bars and their orientation; the contact markers are layered after the rays.
32:     """
33:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
34:     H, W = g.shape
